// Leak repro — a `class` declared inside a function forms a cycle through the
// call environment: the constructor's closure keeps the env alive (directly
// and via the instance methods hidden inside build_instance), while the env's
// binding keeps the class value alive. Reference counting can never break it.
// Do not delete. Both backends now reclaim it per call: the interpreter via
// its precise gc_refs cycle collector (InterpGC walks the constructor's hidden
// captured method closures via FunctionValue::for_each_captured_value), the
// JIT via its class-in-fn handling. Before the fix the interpreter leaked
// ~2 objects/call (env + class value) with no backstop = an unbounded leak.
//
// Each work() re-declares the class 100 times so the ~2-object/call leak is
// amplified well past the noise (~6000 over 30 iters pre-fix, unbounded at
// scale). Threshold `< 1000`: the interpreter is precise (returns ~0); the
// JIT's conservative backstop may retain the most-recent batch, matching the
// sibling gc-leak tests. `< 1000` clears both post-fix with margin.
fn measure(work) {
  work()
  let base = GC.stat().live_objects
  mut i = 0
  while i < 30 { work(); i = i + 1 }
  GC.stat().live_objects - base
}
fn make_a_class() {
  class Local {
    new(v) { this.v = v }
    a() { this.v }
    b() { this.v + 1 }
  }
  Local.new(1)
}
assert_lt(measure(fn () {
  mut j = 0
  while j < 100 { make_a_class().b(); j = j + 1 }
  j
}), 1000)
puts("gc leak [class-in-fn]: no leak")

// Variant — binding the constructor (or any method) to a name goes through
// _wrap_method_with_this, whose closure hides the underlying function (holding
// the class's env). Without exposing it (for_each_captured_value on the
// wrapper) `let mk = Cls.new` leaked ~2 objects/call even bound-but-uncalled.
fn make_and_bind() {
  class Local {
    new(v) { this.v = v }
    m() { this.v }
  }
  let mk = Local.new     // wrapper over the ctor — the leak site
  mk(1).m()
}
assert_lt(measure(fn () {
  mut j = 0
  while j < 100 { make_and_bind(); j = j + 1 }
  j
}), 1000)
puts("gc leak [wrapped-ctor bound to name]: no leak")
